{"id":"01a0657e-01e1-7bbe-b017-c797da978208","chapterSlug":"rw8-54 H","paragraph":441,"wording":"[Gladiator]","event":"named","holderSlug":"yvlon","holderQuote":"Both Yvlon and Mectail were criminals of Nerrhavia’s Fallen who’d been shuffled into the [Gladiator] ring. Yvlon grimaced, and Mectail nodded, tapping his own neckband. Not as painful as a collar, but…it boiled her blood. And that was despite Yvlon having a wooden one since all the enchanted, metal ones kept breaking."}
{"id":"01a0657e-01e1-79bf-87a3-91d7d2b5893d","chapterSlug":"rw8-54 H","paragraph":452,"wording":"[Gladiator]","event":"named","holderSlug":"yvlon","holderQuote":"It was a sight. Yvlon Byres had to admit, grudgingly, that most of the warriors in the Coliseum of Monarchs could go toe-to-toe with a lot of Gold-ranks she’d seen, just on pure weapon skill alone. And they had levels to match—but in that [Gladiator] class, which she now knew to be part show."}
